The personality dialog now switches Direct and Smart with the relay toggle. The form still stores the channel constants `smart` and `direct`, and a new personality still starts on Smart.

**Smart is on the left, Direct on the right.** That is the same left-to-right order the radio group already used. The switch points at the selected word: `toggle-switch-left.png` while the control holds `smart`, `toggle-switch-right.png` while it holds `direct`.

```93:97:src/app/voice-assistant/voice-assistant.component.html
                            [src]="
                                channelPointsRight
                                    ? '../../assets/toggle-switch-right.png'
                                    : '../../assets/toggle-switch-left.png'
                            "
```

`channelPointsRight` is true only when the form control equals `DIRECT_CHANNEL`. Clicking the button flips that control between the two constants. There is no `[disabled]` state.

When `showSmartChannelControl` is false, that whole block is omitted. The dialog keeps the existing Direct-only text (`LBL_Channel_Direct`, and the offline explanation when the on-device model is selected). `defaultChannel()` still returns Direct, and saving a new personality still writes Direct. Nothing offers a switch that cannot switch.

**Add** opens on Smart, with the knob pointing left. **Edit** shows the personality’s stored channel. Both are covered by the spec `points the channel toggle at Smart by default and at a stored channel when editing`: a stored Direct personality shows the right-pointing image, a stored Smart personality the left-pointing one.

The new control:

```html
<div class="col text-end">
    <span class="align-middle" id="label-channel-smart">Smart</span>
</div>
<div class="col pe-0 ps-0">
    <button
        class="btn border-0 p-0"
        id="channel-toggle"
        data-test="TGL_Channel"
        type="button"
        (click)="toggleChannel()">
        <img
            [src]="
                channelPointsRight
                    ? '../../assets/toggle-switch-right.png'
                    : '../../assets/toggle-switch-left.png'
            "
            alt="Toggle for switching the chat channel between Direct and Smart" />
    </button>
</div>
<div class="col text-start">
    <span class="align-middle" id="label-channel-direct">Direct</span>
</div>
```

`grep -n "RBN_Channel_" src/app/voice-assistant/voice-assistant.component.html` prints no matches. The radio markup is gone.

